<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42873" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scantĭus</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a</i>, <i>name of a
			Roman</i> gens. So, Scantia, <i>a woman abused by
				Clodius</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Mil. 27, 75</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scantĭus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>Scantian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">silva,</span>”
				<i>in Campania</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Agr. 1, 1, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 4, 15</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquae, perh. in the same place,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					2, 107, 111, § 240</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scantĭānus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Scantian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mala,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 7, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">7, 143</span></i>
			<i>fin.</i>; <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 59, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 15, 14, 15, § 50</span></i>
			(Jahn, Scandianus): vitis, Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Plin. 14, 4,
				5, § 47</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
